\DOC PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC

\TYPE {PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC : ?public_vars:term list -> thm * (thm option array) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
A complete decision procedure for constant-time/safety specification goals: it
discharges an existentially quantified event-trace specification goal outright.

\DESCRIBE
The optional argument {public_vars : term list} lists the terms naming the
variables treated as public, i.e. those the event function may depend on; {exec
: thm * (thm option array)} is the execution record for the program under
analysis, consisting of a theorem giving the length of the machine-code list
together with an array of per-instruction decoding theorems. It applies to a
goal whose postcondition asserts that the emitted event trace equals {f_events}
applied to some of the quantified variables and satisfies a
memory-access-inbounds condition:
{
   ?- ?f_events. !x1 ... xn. t ==> ensures ...
   =============================================  PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC public_vars exec
}
{
   
}
\noindent so the goal is proved completely, leaving nothing behind and
introducing no new assumptions.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single outcome, on assumption-free goals of
exactly this existential/universal {ensures} safety-specification shape.

\ENDDOC
